{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.FeynmanPathIntegrals.MarkovIdentificationInstance","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.FeynmanPathIntegrals.MarkovIdentificationInstance","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.FeynmanPathIntegrals.markov_identification","lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.MarkovTraceInstance","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Fin"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FeynmanPathIntegrals.markov_identification_of_markovTrace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FeynmanPathIntegrals.markov_identification_of_markovTrace","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FeynmanPathIntegrals/MarkovIdentificationInstance.lean#L113-L124","doc":"`lem:feynman-markov-identification`, unconditionally at convention D: the Markov-weighted\neigenbasis amplitude built from the Ocneanu weights and the seminormal block traces equals the\nMarkov trace of `x`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FeynmanPathIntegrals.markovTrace_branching_of_markovTrace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FeynmanPathIntegrals.markovTrace_branching_of_markovTrace","kind":"theorem","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FeynmanPathIntegrals/MarkovIdentificationInstance.lean#L97-L111","doc":"**The branching identity, proved at the Markov-trace data.** For any Markov trace `T` at `z_D`\nand any `x ∈ H_{n+1}(q)`: with the blocks indexed by `diagIndex`, the weights the Ocneanu weights,\nthe partial traces the seminormal block traces of `x`, and the Markov trace `T.tr n x`,\n`markovTrace_branching` holds — it is derived, not supplied. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FeynmanPathIntegrals.markovTrace_eq_weighted_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FeynmanPathIntegrals.markovTrace_eq_weighted_sum","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FeynmanPathIntegrals/MarkovIdentificationInstance.lean#L87-L95","doc":"**The branching decomposition, as a theorem.** Every Markov trace at `z_D` is the\nOcneanu-weighted sum of the seminormal per-block traces. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FeynmanPathIntegrals.indexed_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FeynmanPathIntegrals.indexed_mul","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FeynmanPathIntegrals/MarkovIdentificationInstance.lean#L79-L83","doc":"Transport respects pointwise products. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FeynmanPathIntegrals.sum_indexed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FeynmanPathIntegrals.sum_indexed","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FeynmanPathIntegrals/MarkovIdentificationInstance.lean#L73-L77","doc":"The range sum of the transported function is the Fintype sum over blocks. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FeynmanPathIntegrals.indexed_of_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FeynmanPathIntegrals.indexed_of_lt","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FeynmanPathIntegrals/MarkovIdentificationInstance.lean#L68-L71","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FeynmanPathIntegrals.indexed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FeynmanPathIntegrals.indexed","kind":"def","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FeynmanPathIntegrals/MarkovIdentificationInstance.lean#L64-L66","doc":"Transport a function on blocks to a function on `ℕ`, zero off-range. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FeynmanPathIntegrals.diagIndex","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FeynmanPathIntegrals.diagIndex","kind":"def","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FeynmanPathIntegrals/MarkovIdentificationInstance.lean#L60-L62","doc":"An enumeration of the blocks by a natural index. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FeynmanPathIntegrals.Diag","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FeynmanPathIntegrals.Diag","kind":"def","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FeynmanPathIntegrals/MarkovIdentificationInstance.lean#L57-L58","doc":"The Young diagrams of size `n + 1` — the Wedderburn blocks of `H_{n+1}(q)`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}